<title>NETHERLANDS: PHILIPS DECLINES VIRTUALITY BID COMMENT.</title>
<headline>PHILIPS DECLINES VIRTUALITY BID COMMENT.</headline>
<dateline>EINDHOVEN, Netherlands 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philips Electronics NV on Friday declined to comment on speculation in the London stock market it had UK virtual reality systems firm Virtuality Group Plc in its sights as a bid target.</p>
<p>&quot;We never comment on market rumours,&quot; a Philips spokeswoman said, confirming the company had a very small stake in the firm.</p>
<p>&quot;There are some things we're discussing with them at the moment but that's product related,&quot; she added. &quot;Whether that's causing the speculation I don't know.&quot;</p>
<p>London share traders earlier said Virtuality extended recent strong gains on talk of a possible Philips takeover bid.</p>
<p>Philips shares closed 1.80 guilders lower at 73.60 guilders, falling in line with a generally lower Amsterdam bourse.</p>
<p>Virtuality earlier climbed 1-1/2p to 76-1/2p in London on the speculation.</p>
